      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes a mechanism that records the prior state of files before the guarded tool executor overwrites them. Here\u0027s what it does:\n\n**Core function**: Before any file is overwritten, the system journals (records) its previous state \u2014 either the prior content if the file existed, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If an agent run fails (due to a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order:\n- Restoring previous content for files that already existed\n- Deleting any newly created files\n\n**Transaction semantics**: This gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without needing a database \u2014 the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of one run.\n\n**Query agent exception**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the journal\u0027s rollback functionality because it has no write tool at all, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
